            "text": "{\"primary_meaning\":\"A religious group or institution that claims to serve God and hold true covenantal authority, but actively opposes Christ and persecutes true believers. In its original biblical context, it specifically refers to local Jewish communities in Asia Minor who rejected Jesus as Messiah and persecuted the early Christians, while 'assembly of the wicked' prophetically describes those who orchestrated the crucifixion.\",\"primary_basis\":[\"Revelation 2:9\",\"Revelation 3:9\",\"Psalm 22:16\",\"John 8:44\"],\"alternatives\":[{\"meaning\":\"Any false church, heretical group, or apostate religious institution that opposes true believers (a general spiritualized application historically used by Protestant Reformers against the Papacy).\",\"basis\":[\"Revelation 2:9\",\"Revelation 3:9\"],\"prominence\":\"common\"},{\"meaning\":\"A historical anti-Semitic designation for the Jewish people collectively across all time.\",\"basis\":[\"John 8:44\",\"Revelation 2:9\"],\"prominence\":\"minority\"},{\"meaning\":\"Literal occult gatherings or groups explicitly worshipping Satan.\",\"basis\":[\"Revelation 2:9\"],\"prominence\":\"rare\"}],\"has_settled_consensus\":true,\"confidence\":\"high\",\"notes\":\"Modern biblical scholarship largely agrees that 'synagogue of Satan' originally described specific first-century local conflicts between early Christians and established Jewish communities in Smyrna and Philadelphia, rather than serving as a blanket condemnation of all Jews. 'Assembly of the wicked' is primarily drawn from Psalm 22:16, traditionally read as a Messianic prophecy regarding Christ's executioners.\"}",
